NXR-154|ARM register and alignment validation|Verification|The Cortex-M3 simulation stress shall check callee-saved state across blocking SVC and integer register plus NZCV state across interrupt-only regions, including injected mismatch detection and PSP padding.|Arithmetic workloads do not explicitly exercise every saved register or the exception alignment flag.|Distinct canaries pass, injected r7 mismatch returns zero, ticks progress in the positive interrupt harness, and four-byte PSP alignment produces the hardware padding flag.|Three QEMU timer shifts per configured stress image.|NXR-150|Assembly harnesses preserve AAPCS caller state and avoid C calls on a deliberately misaligned stack.|No heap; validation-only stack frames removed from ordinary images when unreferenced.|ports/arm-mps2/canaries.S,ports/arm-mps2/rtos_port.hpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp,docs/arm-canaries.rst|Simulation coverage only, not MCU qualification or complete instruction-state proof.|ports/arm-mps2/canaries.S,ports/arm-mps2/rtos_port.hpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp|examples/arm_stress.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
NXR-155|ARM timer catch-up and rollover variants|Verification|ARM simulation shall exercise masked multi-period timer catch-up, an initial 32-bit counter rollover with unchanged reload modulus, and varied queue capacity and tick rate.|Pending IRQ bits do not count missed periods and short timer reloads break software wrap extension.|Ticks remain unchanged while masked then catch up within a counter deadline; near-wrap and faster-tick presets pass finite message and semaphore workloads.|QEMU normal, near-wrap and faster-tick runs with retained logs.|NXR-150|CMSDK timer initial value configurable separately from full 32-bit reload; stress follows configured tick rate.|No dynamic firmware storage; variant queue capacity fixed at compilation.|ports/arm-mps2/rtos_port.hpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp,CMakePresets.json,cmake/firmware.cmake,docs/arm-canaries.rst|Counter extension still requires serialized reads more often than a full 32-bit period; no hardware timing guarantee.|ports/arm-mps2/rtos_port.hpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp,cmake/firmware.cmake|examples/arm_stress.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
